From d9a9645d5b1adeef33f227f871493b702155c3a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: architecture review <review@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:33:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] D9 spike: the knowledge_service principal, a closed non-Lead
 committer (ADR-0013 Q1)

Review branch on top of the T4 prototype, built after the designer accepted
ADR-0013 question 1: one project-scoped service principal with its own
credential kind may commit only the knowledge.* transaction family, holds no
Lead authority, and survives Lead handoff and takeover.

- control.schema.json: token kind `service`.
- engine/authority.py: SERVICE_FAMILIES, issue_service_token (rotation is
  re-issuance), require_service (no generation check), credential_kind.
- engine/closure.py (new): the closed family table; the control store
  enforces it at commit by comparing the committed state with the one to be
  written (keys, counters, record paths, op prefix). TRANSACTION_CLOSURE.
- engine/base.py: TxnContext.archival; Kernel.service_txn and actor_txn.
- engine/archive_ops.py: a non-archival transaction appends its own entries
  and archives nothing, ends no credential, prunes nothing.
- engine/service_ops.py, cli/service_commands.py: `aew service
  issue|revoke|show` (issue and revoke are Lead transitions).
- engine/knowledge_ops.py, cli/knowledge_commands.py: knowledge commands
  route by credential kind; AEW_SERVICE_TOKEN; the result names the actor.
- harness/lead_broker.py: `service issue` is credential-emitting.
- tests: invariants rule 30; the dispatch registry classifies the service
  commands; test_service_identity.py (8 tests, the takeover one on a pty).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
